# Code quality

- Use early returns to avoid nesting beyond 2 levels.
- Extract any function longer than ~30 lines into named helpers.
- Boolean variables/props are prefixed `is`, `has`, or `should`
  (e.g. `isInvited`, `hasActiveGrant`).
- Named exports only — no default exports for components, hooks, or
  utilities.
- No comments that restate what the code does. Comment only WHY, when the
  reason isn't obvious from names (e.g. "snapshot price to avoid retroactive
  billing changes").
- Prefer composition over inheritance; no class hierarchies.
- Every exported function has an explicit return type — do not rely on
  inference for public API surfaces.
- Do not add a library, dependency, or new pattern (state manager, ORM,
  form lib) that isn't already in `package.json` without asking first.
